Built standalone, stdlib-only compress.py supporting both requested commands. It losslessly packs structured records, hexadecimal data, and base-36 strings, with a bz2 fallback for other inputs. The corpus round-trips byte-identically: 44,267 bytes compress to 16,853 bytes, a 61.9288% reduction, beating default zlib’s 22,390 bytes. The registered assay checks the command-line round trip and repeated in-memory round trips before printing the score; additional binary and edge-case tests passed.